nd, watch, share and create content more easily. These test features (sometimes also called “betas” or “experiments”) are usually available for a short period of time and only for a small group of people.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\n\\u003cdiv\\u003eIf you ever notice that YouTube looks a bit different for you than it does for your friend or family member, you’re likely seeing one of these experiments. Be sure to \\u003ca href\x3d\\\x22https://support.google.com/youtube/answer/4347644\\\x22 target\x3d\\\x22_blank\\\x22 rel\x3d\\\x22noopener\\\x22\\u003egive YouTube feedback\\u003c/a\\u003e and report any potential technical issues – our teams use this information and experiment results to help us decide if, when, and how to release these features more broadly.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\n\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003cb\\u003eLearn more about \\u003ci\\u003esome\\u003c/i\\u003e existing feature experiments\\u003c/b\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\\n\\u003cdiv\\u003eTo help you keep up with these test features, our TeamYouTube Community Managers will pilot keeping this forum thread updated with cool and interesting ones that we think you’ll want to know about! While this post won’t include every experiment, it’s a good place to start if you’re curious about what we’re testing out, or whether or not you’re currently seeing an experiment. To learn about previous experiments, \\u003ca href\x3d\\\x22https://support.google.com/youtube/thread/162258829?hl\x3den\\\x22 target\x3d\\\x22_blank\\\x22 rel\x3d\\\x22noopener\\\x22\\u003echeck out this post\\u003c/a\\u003e.\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\x22,\x22en\x22,40,[[\x22platform\x22,\x22web\x22],[\x22User_type\x22,\x22viewer\x22]],1778177486966291,null,null,1721849368671745,1,\x22watch_discover\x22,0,100,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[null,null,13928,1580157720660593,6],[null,null,13928,1580157858934384,5],[null,null,13928,1580165017680060,6],[null,nu