3c/div\\u003e\x22,[],[1,null,null,1720446298755267,124823467],null,null,null,null,null,null,100,null,null,null,1720446298755267,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[null,0.84214675426483154,0,\x22CiQ0YzI5YTFkYS1kMTkwLTY3ODMtYzRmMy1iNjc1NjQ2MjBjZDEQBBgF\x22,\x221:06d39463-f12a-d9b5-d5ea-8ae7fa4051f7\x22],null,null,null,null,\x22en\x22],null,[[\x22Meaghan - TeamYouTube\x22,\x22https://storage.googleapis.com/support-forums-api/avatar/profile-124823467-12584882851192598979.jpeg\x22,1631041764776775,\x22\x22,\x22\x22,\x22\x22,\x22\x22],[null,1631140707065836,100,null,[7]],124823467,1],[null,null,0,0],0,null,[],[],null,[]]],[null,[62,\x221720446298755267\x22,\x221765904954976843\x22,0]],[[[[395263454,\x221765904954976843\x22,18138167,1765904955751416],null,300126495,\x22\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003cb\\u003e[December 16, 2025] Exploring Portraits on YouTube with participating creators:\\u003c/b\\u003e Over the last several months, Google Labs has been experimenting with \\u003ca href\x3d\\\x22https://labs.google/portraits/\\\x22 target\x3d\\\x22_blank\\\x22 rel\x3d\\\x22noopener\\\x22\\u003ePortraits\\u003c/a\\u003e. This experimental feature lets viewers conversationally interact with AI representations of participating creators and gives these creators insights into topics that their audiences are interested in. Viewers can engage with Portraits to learn more about topics directly related to participating creators’ content, and creators can share their unique knowledge through this new, interactive format.\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003cbr\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003eBased on the feedback from the initial Google Labs experiment, we’re expanding the feature to a small group of YouTube creators who have specifically chosen to participate. These creators have provided the content and sources that their Portraits are built on. U.S. viewers 18 years or older watching YouTube on desktop may see the option to “Talk to Creator’s Portrait” on a participating creator’s channel, where viewers can engage with the creator’s Portrait by asking questions and exploring topics related to their content. We’ll be monitoring feedback in response to Portraits closely and we’ll keep our community updated on any related news.\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003cbr\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\x22,[],[1,null,null,1765904954976843,300126495],null,null,null,null,null,null,100,null,null,null,1765904954976843,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[null,0.89942938089370728,0,\x22CiRkZTgzOTg5OC01MDY4LTg0NGQtZTA0ZS04YWRmNGQ4NGNmMzYQBBgF\x22,\x221:0d71e7cb-8aeb-840c-cde1-a56376d7ab8f\x22],null,null,null,null,\x22en\x22],null,[[\x22Hank (TeamYouTube)\x22,\x22https://storage.googleapis.com/support-forums-api/avatar/profile-300126495-16293678855050489375.png\x22,1727983350823558,\x22\x22,\x22\x22,\x22\x22,\x22\x22],[null,1729031807257791,100,null,[7]],300126495,1],[null,null,0,0],0,null,[],[],null,[]]],[[[[395266028,\x221765906021564579\x22,18138167,1765906031118656],null,47860568,\x22\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003cb\\u003e[December 16, 2025] Testing image posts in the Shorts feed:\\u003c/b\\u003e We’re experimenting with showing image posts in the Shorts feed to help creators reach their audience with posts in a new place. Creators can include up to 10 images in their posts, making them a great way to tell a story.\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003cbr\\u003eCreators: All image posts created through the “Create” button may be shown in the Shorts feed during this test. Learn more about creating posts \\u003ca href\x3d\\\x22https://support.google.com/youtube/answer/7124474?hl\x3den\\u0026amp;ref_topic\x3d9257790\\u0026amp;sjid\x3d17490125299596337965-NC\\u0026amp;co\x3dGENIE.Platform%3DDesktop\\u0026amp;oco\x3d1\\\x22 target\x3d\\\x22_blank\\\x22 rel\x3d\\\x22noopener\\\x22\\u003ehere\\u003c/a\\u003e. We know audio is an important tool to help you express yourself and tell your story, so we’ll keep everyone updated as we explore testing music with this experience.\x22,[],[1,null,null,1765906021564579,47860568],null,null,null,null,null,1765906030604307,100,null,null,47860568,1765906021564579,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[null,0.86819988489151,0,\x22CiRlM2M4ZTQwMS0zOWE5LTg2MjctZGMxYS04M2UwOWE1OTY1YTkQBBgF\x22,\x221:e665c3c7-9da1-ddeb-1b42-a09dfd2c2423\x22],null,null,null,null,\x22en\x22],null,[[\x22Jensen - TeamYouTube\x22,\x22https://storage.googleapis.com/support-forums-api/avatar/profile-47860568-15295992705602100594.png\x22,1589917228839848],[null,1590574074888732,100,null,[7]],47860568,1],[null,null,0,0],0,null,[],[],null,[[\x22Jensen - TeamYouTube\x22,\x22https://storage.googleapis.com/support-forums-api/avatar/profile-47860568-15295992705602100594.png\x22,1589917228839848],[null,1590574074888732,100,null,[7]],47860568,1]]],[[[[395732929,\x221766081353084954\x22,18138167,1766082883934566],null,6555956,\x22\\u003cb\\u003e[December 18, 2025] Testing a new location and functionality for the Dislike button on Shorts:\\u003c/b\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;Since launching Shorts, we’ve been listening closely to your feedback on how to improve the viewing experience. We’ve heard that you often use “Dislike” and “Not interested” interchangeably on Shorts, or aren’t sure what the differences are. To address this, and to better match with how people typically interact with short-form video feeds today, we’re experimenting with options where “Dislike” and “Not Interested” are merged into one \\\x22thumbs down\\\x22 icon behind the 3 dot menu.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003cbr\\u003e\\u003cbr\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003eThis means some viewers will see the “thumbs down” icon titled as “Dislike” and others will see it titled as “Not Interested.” All viewers in the experiment who click “thumbs down” on a Short will receive an optional feedback survey, similar to how “Not Interested” works today.\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003cbr\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003eWe\x27re hoping this will make it clearer on how to tune your Shorts recommendations. \\u003ca href\x3d\\\x22https://support.google.com/youtube/answer/4347644?hl\x3den\\u0026amp;co\x3dGENIE.Platform%3DAndroid\\\x22 target\x3d\\\x22_blank\\\x22 rel\x3d\\\x22noopener\\\x22\\u003eYou can also share your feedback about this experiment here\\u003c/a\\u003e, and we’ll keep you posted on future updates.\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003cbr\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003cimg src\x3d\\\x22//storage.googleapis.com/support-forums-api/attachment/message-395732929-13739404955593195575.png\\\x22\\u003e\x22,[],[1,null,null,1766082883934566,149071703],[3,null,[6555956,1766081353084954],1766081353084954,6555956],null,[[\x22https://storage.googleapis.com/support-forums-api/attachment/message-395732929-13739404955593195575.png\x22,\x22shorts-dislike-removal.png\x22,244323,\x22image/png\x22,null,null,null,\x22message-395732929-13739404955593195575\x22,1]],null,null,null,100,null,null,null,1766081353084954,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[null,0.88786685466766357,0,\x22CiRlMGVhNTE0Mi03Yzg4LTcwYzEtZDY4OC1iZjMwYjBjN2U1Y2IQBBgF\x22,\x221:26a26da1-641c-17ab-d1ec-4f3441684289\x22],null,null,null,null,\x22en\x22],null,[[\x22Sarah (TeamYouTube)\x22,\x22https://storage.googleapis.com/support-forums-api/avatar/profile-6555956-2987668759732766235.gif\x22,1558473569631906],[null,1558473569631906,100,null,[7]],6555956,1],[null,null,87,2],0,null,[],[],null,[]]],[[[[409337144,\x221770846677237559\x22,18138167,1770846677601702],null,300126495,\x22\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003cb\\u003e[February 11, 2026]\\u0026nbsp;\\u003ca href\x3d\\\x22https://support.google.com/youtube/thread/18138167?hl\x3den\\u0026amp;msgid\x3d333836208\\u0026amp;sjid\x3d12741373669088535116-NC\\\x22 target\x3d\\\x22_blank\\\x22 rel\x3d\\\x22noopener\\\x22\\u003eTesting improved notifications experiences\\u003c/a\\u003e:\\u0026nbsp;\\u003c/b\\u003eWe’re continuing to run a small experiment that will impact viewers who are subscribed to a channel and have set the notifications to “All” for the channel. Here’s what we’re testing:\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003cbr\\u003e\\u003cul\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003eViewers who haven’t recently engaged with a channel, despite having been sent recent push notifications, will not receive\\u0026nbsp;push\\u0026nbsp;notifications in the experiment. Notifications will still be available via the\\u0026nbsp;notification inbox\\u0026nbsp;in the YouTube app, and content will still be viewable on the Subscriptions feed on both desktop and mobile.\\u0026nbsp; Channels that upload infrequently will not have their notifications affected.\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003eActively engaged viewers with push notifications enabled on their device will continue to receive them. (No change)\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\u003cbr\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003eViewers often opt in to receive \\\x22All\\\x22 notifications from many channels. When they feel overwhelmed or are no longer interested in a specific channel, instead of\\u0026nbsp;\\u003ca href\x3d\\\x22https://support.google.com/youtube/answer/3382248\\\x22 target\x3d\\\x22_blank\\\x22 rel\x3d\\\x22noopener\\\x22\\u003eupdating their subscription and notifications\\u0026nbsp;\\u003c/a\\u003eto better reflect their preferences, they simply turn off all notifications from the YouTube app entirely. It’s common for users to have turned on All notifications for a channel, only to have turned off app-level notifications (Creators\\u0026nbsp;\\u003ca href\x3d\\\x22https://support.google.com/youtube/answer/9336507\\\x22 target\x3d\\\x22_blank\\\x22 rel\x3d\\\x22noopener\\\x22\\u003ecan see how this impacts their channel\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;in the Audience tab).\\u0026nbsp;\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003cbr\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003eWhen viewers turn off all notifications from YouTube, all creators are unable to reach even their most engaged viewers outside the app. The goal of this experiment is to help us find ways to reduce this problem.\\u003c/div\\u003e\x22,[],[1,null,null,1770846677237559,300126495],null,null,null,null,null,null,100,null,null,null,1770846677237559,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[null,0.88875067234039307,0,\x22CiQxZjUwNGZjMy1kY2I5LWRlNjktMzJmYy1mYzNhMzVjNmVjYjMQBBgF\x22,\x221:0c6fbe4b-0fbf-9d6e-39ba-0120f02e0fae\x22],null,null,null,null,\x22en\x22],null,[[\x22Hank (TeamYouTube)\x22,\x22https://storage.googleapis.com/support-forums-api/avatar/profile-300126495-16293678855050489375.png\x22,1727983350823558,\x22\x22,\x22\x22,\x22\x22,\x22\x22],[null,1729031807257791,100,null,[7]],300126495,1],[null,null,0,0],0,null,[],[],null,[]]],[[[[411145985,\x221771436524312803\x22,18138167,1771436524579439],null,300126495,\x22\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003cb\\u003e[Feb 18, 2026] Testing the conversational AI tool on TV’s:\\u003c/b\\u003e We’re experimenting with bringing \\u003ca href\x3d\\\x22https://support.google.com/youtube/answer/14110396?hl\x3den\\\x22 target\x3d\\\x22_blank\\\x22 rel\x3d\\\x22noopener\\\x22\\u003eYouTube’s conversational AI tool\\u003c/a\\u003e to smart TVs, gaming consoles, and streaming devices! If you’re eligible, here’s how to access it:\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003cbr\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003col\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003eWhile watching a video, select the \\u003ca href\x3d\\\x22https://support.google.com/youtube/answer/14110396?hl\x3den\\\x22 target\x3d\\\x22_blank\\\x22 rel\x3d\\\x22noopener\\\x22\\u003e“Ask” button\\u003c/a\\u003e to open the AI tool\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003eSelect from suggested prompts, or use the microphone button to ask questions using your voice\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003c/ol\\u003e\\u003cbr\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003eIf your TV remote has a microphone button, you can also use that button to trigger th